                    \\mathcal{R}_{\mathbf{X}}
                    \\otimes
                    \\mathcal{S}_{\mathbf{X}}
                    \\big)_{y}
                    \\;,\;
                    \\mathcal{T}_{y}
                    \\Big)
                    \&amp;
                    \\text{ by definition }
                    \\\
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    Func(\mathbf{X},\mathbf{V})
                    \\big(
                    \\mathcal{R}_{\mathbf{X}}
                    \\otimes
                    \\mathcal{S}_{\mathbf{X}}
                    \\;,\;
                    \\mathcal{T}_{\mathbf{X}}
                    \\big)
                    \&amp;
                    \\text{ by definition, }
                    \\end{array}
            %p where we used, apart from the above definitions:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  that
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom-functors+preserve+limits"} internal hom-functors preserve limits
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a{:href => "end#Fubini"} Fubini theorem for ends
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-Yoneda+lemma"} co-Yoneda lemma
            %p
              This establishes that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [-,-]
              is an internal hom in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Func
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Func(\mathbf{X},\mathbf{V})
              for the objectwise tensor product, as claimed.
            %p
              The natural isomorphisms needed to exhibit the (co)tensoring of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
